From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Radsat Developers <dev@radsat.local>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 19:40:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] watchdog: quiet nowayout warn during SYSTEM_RESTART

Userspace intentionally arms omap_wdt without magic-close before reboot
so a hung flush still resets the SoC. The core "watchdog did not stop!"
warning looks like a failure; skip it when we are already restarting.

---
diff --git a/drivers/watchdog/watchdog_dev.c b/drivers/watchdog/watchdog_dev.c
--- a/drivers/watchdog/watchdog_dev.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/watchdog_dev.c
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
 #include <linux/errno.h>	/* error codes */
 #include <linux/fs.h>		/* everything... */
 #include <linux/kernel.h>	/* printk() */
+#include <linux/reboot.h>	/* system_state */
 #include <linux/kmod.h>		/* request_module() */
 #include <linux/kthread.h>	/* kthread_run / wake_up_process */
 #include <linux/miscdevice.h>	/* misc_register and friends */
@@ -355,8 +356,10 @@ static int watchdog_release(struct inode *inode, struct file *file)
 	 * make sure that a machine reboot happens.
 	 */
 	if (test_bit(WDOG_ACTIVE, &wdd->status)) {
-		pr_crit("watchdog%d: watchdog did not stop!\n", wdd->id);
+		if (system_state != SYSTEM_RESTART)
+			pr_crit("watchdog%d: watchdog did not stop!\n", wdd->id);
 		watchdog_ping(wdd);
 	}
 
 	/* make sure that /dev/watchdog can be re-opened */
